'
' ===============================================================================
' GIGALAGA - phase 1: a classic Galaga-style formation shooter           
' ===============================================================================
' Engine from DIB_Sync: 32-bit DIB section, direct pixel writes, StretchBlt (COLORONCOLOR) scaling with
' letterbox, timeGetTime loop, resolution dialog. The game renders at the arcade's 224x288 and is scaled up by an
' integer factor, so pixels stay crisp.
'
' Controls : LEFT/RIGHT (or A/D) move, SPACE / CTRL / Z / X fire (hold = auto-fire), P pause, M mute, ESC quit.
'
' Phase 1 contains : title screen, starfield, player ship (2 shots on screen), 5 entry waves flying along curved
'   paths into a swaying/breathing 40-enemy formation (4 bosses, 16 butterflies, 20 bees), dive attacks with aimed
'   shots, boss with 2 hits, explosions, score / high score / extra lives / stage counter, game over.
' Phases 2-3: sound effects and music, all synthesised by the program itself (waveOut, no resources). M = mute.
' Phase 4: high score + settings saved in gigalaga.sav (current directory), C = CRT scanlines (off / light / strong).
' Phase 5: bonus "challenging" stages (stages 5, 10, 15 ...): 40 enemies fly through, nobody shoots, 100 per hit,
'   all 40 = PERFECT + 10000.
' Phase 6: boss tractor beam, captured fighter, rescue and dual fighter.
' Phase 7: warp between stages (stars stretch into streaks), shots / hits / accuracy stats, respawn flash
'   (ideas taken from the way XGalaga does level changes and respawns).
' Phase 8: smarter enemies: dives get more frequent / numerous / faster as the formation thins (the last 6 all attack),
'   6 different dive manoeuvres (more unlock with the stage), bosses take up to 2 butterflies along (kill = 800 / 1600).
' Phase 9: power-up prizes dropped by shot-down divers: S spread, R rapid fire, H shield, V speed, L lemon (bad), 1UP.
' Phase 10: top-8 score table with 3-letter name entry (saved), attract-mode title pages (scores, points, power-ups,
'   controls; LEFT / RIGHT flips pages), mouse steering (move the mouse, left button fires) and gamepad (joyGetPosEx).
'   They are lost when the ship is lost. 8 player bullet slots.
' Phase 11: wave variety: 12 entry patterns picked per stage (stage 1 keeps the classic five), entries speed up with the
'   stage, 3 more dive manoeuvres (spin, diagonal drift, double-back).
' Phase 12: visual pack: 4 enemy skins (new colours every 4 stages, new hornet / moth silhouettes later), shield bubble,
'   thruster flame + banking ship, bigger explosions, pixel-art title logo, bouncing PAUSED banner, scrolling title
'   ticker, Q = end the current game.
' Phase 13: the 15 XGalaga levels (.xgl): compass-step paths and per-slot launch delays, used on every other stage
'   (mapped onto our 40 slots by dropping the level's last row); the other stages keep the random recipes.
' Phase 14: difficulty selector (keys + and - on the title screen): Easy / Normal / Hard, saved in gigalaga.sav.
'
$INCLUDE "windowssdk.inc"

AUTODEFINE "Off"

